<div class="main-title">
  <h1>Likutay Halachos</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">Evven Ha-Ezer &bull; Hilchos Ishus &bull; Halacha 2</div>
</div>

<div class="halacha-title">
  <h2>Halacha 1</h2>
</div>

<div class="halacha-preface">
In Hilchos Pirya V&rsquo;Rivya, Halacha 1.
</div>

<div class="halacha-title">
  <h2>Halacha 2</h2>
</div>

<div class="halacha-preface">
Based on Likutay Moharan II, Torah 8 &mdash; &ldquo;Tik&rsquo;u Tochachah&rdquo; (&ldquo;Blow [the Shofar] &mdash; A Reproof&rdquo;).
</div>

<p class="para"><b>A Kohein, a Levi, and a Yisra&rsquo;el are permitted to intermarry with one another, and the offspring follows the male:</b></p>

<h3 class="oas-heading" id="oas-1">Oas Alef</h3>

<p class="para">For it is brought in the Torah &ldquo;Tik&rsquo;u 3&rdquo; which speaks of rebuke (in Likutay Tinyana, Siman 8), that the essential <i>tefillah</i> is compassion and supplications, and the essential compassion depends on <i>da&rsquo;as</i> (knowledge/awareness), etc. And sometimes, when they [the forces of the Other Side] suckle from the compassion, then the compassion is blemished and becomes cruelty, and then the <i>da&rsquo;as</i> is blemished, etc.; see there. And from this comes, G-d forbid, the desire of adultery, for the essential desire comes through the blemish of <i>da&rsquo;as</i>. For the brain is a partition spread out before this desire, for there are three brains, and from them are drawn three kinds of compassion, which are the aspect of three <i>tefillos</i> (prayers) per day. And each of the three brains is the aspect of a partition spread out before this desire, etc.; see there.</p>

<p class="para">And then the <i>tefillah</i> is in the aspect of <i>din</i> (judgment), etc. And then one needs a person of great power who can pray <i>tefillah</i> in the aspect of <i>din</i>, like Pinchas at the time of the deed of Zimri, etc. For this <i>tefillah</i> of the man of great power stands at the throat of the <i>Sitra Achara</i> until it is compelled to vomit forth all the <i>tefillos</i> and the holinesses that it swallowed, in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;The wealth he swallowed he shall vomit up&rdquo;</span> <span class="source-ref">(Iyov 20:15)</span>, etc. And this is the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;You broke apart the sea with Your might; You shattered the heads of the sea-serpents upon the waters&rdquo;</span> <span class="source-ref">(Tehillim 74:13)</span>, the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;For the earth shall be full of the knowledge of Hashem, as the waters cover the sea&rdquo;</span> <span class="source-ref">(Yeshayah 11:9)</span>, etc. And this is the aspect of <i>ananei d&rsquo;shafchei maya</i> (clouds that pour forth water), etc.; see there all of this very well.</p>

<h3 class="oas-heading" id="oas-2">Oas Beis</h3>

<p class="para">And this is the aspect of Kohein, Levi, Yisra&rsquo;el, which are the essential holiness of the <i>yichus</i> (lineage) of Israel. For Israel, a holy nation, must guard themselves that their unions should be in holiness and in purity, for this is the essential holiness of Israel &mdash; to guard oneself from the blemish of the desire of adultery, as is known. And therefore they must guard themselves that their unions should be in great holiness, and that there should not be attached to them, G-d forbid, the aspect of the aforementioned desire.</p>

<p class="para">And the essential guarding from the blemish of this desire is through the three brains, which are partitions spread out before this desire, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of Kohein, Levi, Yisra&rsquo;el, which are the aspect of the three brains &mdash; <i>Chochmah</i>, <i>Binah</i>, <i>Da&rsquo;as</i> &mdash; as is known, which are the aspect of partitions spread out before this desire. And therefore the essential holiness of the union of Israel is through the aspect of Kohein, Levi, Yisra&rsquo;el, which are the essential boundary of holy lineage. For only they alone can unite in holiness as is fitting, so that there should not be attached to their union, G-d forbid, the blemish of the desire of adultery. For Kohein, Levi, Yisra&rsquo;el are the aspect of the aforementioned three brains, which are the aspect of partitions spread out before this desire. And therefore the essential boundary of holy lineage is Kohein, Levi, Yisra&rsquo;el, as is explained in the Mishnah and Shulchan Aruch, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3 class="oas-heading" id="oas-3">Oas Gimmel</h3>

<p class="para">And this is why our Sages, of blessed memory, gave a sign regarding a proper family &mdash; when it is not given to strife and contention. But a family that is given to strife and contention &mdash; this is a sign that there is a blemish of lineage in it, as is brought in the Shulchan Aruch. For compassion depends on <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, as mentioned above in the aforementioned teaching, and one who has no compassion has no <i>da&rsquo;as</i>.</p>

<p class="para">And therefore a family that is given to strife and contention, which is the aspect of anger and harsh judgments, the opposite of compassion &mdash; it is certainly not fitting for the seed of Israel to unite with them, and there is certainly a blemish of lineage in them. For the essential holiness of the lineage of Israel is that they are compassionate ones, children of compassionate ones &mdash; which is the aspect of <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, which is the essential holiness of their lineage, the aspect of Kohein, Levi, Yisra&rsquo;el, the three brains, which are the essential holiness of the <i>bris</i>, as mentioned above. But one who is a person of contention, which is the opposite of compassion, which is a blemish of <i>da&rsquo;as</i> &mdash; it is not fitting to intermarry with him, for he is in the aspect of the blemish of the desire of adultery, which depends on the blemish of <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, which is the blemish of compassion, which is the opposite of the holiness of Kohein, Levi, Yisra&rsquo;el, as mentioned above. And therefore there is certainly a blemish of lineage in him and it is forbidden to intermarry with him, for the essential thing depends on compassion, which is the aspect of <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, which is the partition spread out before this desire, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3 class="oas-heading" id="oas-4">Oas Daled</h3>

<p class="para">And therefore it is forbidden for us to intermarry and to unite with all the nations, for they are all in the aspect of cruelty and <i>din</i> (harsh judgment), for they are compared to wild beasts &mdash; the aspect of cruelty and harsh judgments, which is the blemish of <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, from which comes the aforementioned desire. And therefore it is forbidden for Israel to intermarry with them, for the essential union of Israel must be specifically in the aspect of compassion and <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, which is the partition spread out before the desire, in order that the union should be in holiness as is fitting, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3 class="oas-heading" id="oas-5">Oas Heh</h3>

<p class="para">And therefore there are nations that even when they convert are forbidden to enter the congregation of Hashem. This is because the cruelty and the <i>din</i> have become so attached to them that they cannot be included within the compassion and the <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, which is the aspect of the holiness of Israel, even when they convert.</p>

<p class="para">And this is what our Sages, of blessed memory, said: the <i>Nesinim</i> (Gibeonites) &mdash; David decreed upon them, because they had no compassion at all, as is brought there. He said: There are three signs in this nation &mdash; they are compassionate, they are modest, and they perform acts of kindness. Whoever has these three signs is fit to cleave to [Israel], and whoever does not have these three signs is not fit to cleave to [Israel]. That is, as mentioned above &mdash; for it is not fitting to cleave to the congregation of Hashem, to the holy seed of Israel, except for one who is included within compassion, which is the aspect of <i>da&rsquo;as</i>. But one who has no compassion, such as the <i>Nesinim</i>, is forbidden to enter the congregation of Hashem, for the blemish of compassion is the blemish of <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, which is the aspect of the desire of adultery. For the holy union of Israel must be separated from the blemish of this desire, as mentioned above.</p>

<p class="para">And this is why our Sages, of blessed memory, enumerated three qualities: modest, compassionate, and performers of acts of kindness. They are the aspect of the aforementioned three brains, which are the aspect of the three kinds of compassion, etc., as mentioned above. For modesty too is the aspect of <i>da&rsquo;as</i> and compassion, for the essential modesty depends on <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, as it says: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;They were also not ashamed, neither did they know how to blush&rdquo;</span> <span class="source-ref">(Yirmiyah 6:15)</span>. For the animal, which has no <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, has no shame. And as is also understood in the words of Rabbeinu, of blessed memory, elsewhere, in the teaching &ldquo;Markevos Par&rsquo;oh V&rsquo;Cheilo&rdquo; (Siman 38), that shame depends on <i>da&rsquo;as</i>. Also, shame is the aspect of compassion, the opposite of brazenness, which is the aspect of <i>g&rsquo;vuros</i> and harsh judgments.</p>

<p class="para">It follows that all the three aforementioned qualities &mdash; modest, compassionate, and performers of acts of kindness &mdash; are three qualities of compassion, corresponding to the aspect of the three kinds of compassion mentioned above that come from the three brains, as mentioned above, upon which the essential holiness of the union of Israel depends. And whoever is not included in these three qualities of compassion is forbidden to enter the congregation of Hashem. And therefore it was specifically because of this that the <i>Nesinim</i> were forbidden to enter the congregation, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3 class="oas-heading" id="oas-6">Oas Vav</h3>

<p class="para">And this is the aspect of the prohibition of <i>niddah</i> (menstrual impurity). For the blood of <i>niddah</i> is the aspect of the intense <i>din</i> (harsh judgment) that comes from the contamination of the serpent. And then the union is forbidden, as mentioned above. And the essential <i>tikkun</i> and purification from the blood of <i>niddah</i>, or of the gentiles when they convert and wish to enter the congregation, is through immersion in a <i>mikveh</i>. For the <i>mikveh</i> is the aspect of the waters of <i>da&rsquo;as</i> and compassion, through which comes the essential purification. For the essential prohibition of the blood of <i>niddah</i>, or of uniting with gentiles, is on account of the intensity of <i>din</i>, which is the contamination of the serpent, as mentioned above. And therefore through the <i>mikveh</i>, which is the aspect of the waters of <i>da&rsquo;as</i> and compassion, they are purified, as mentioned above.</p>

<p class="para">For the essential <i>tikkun</i> when the desire of adultery intensifies through the aspect of harsh judgments, G-d forbid, is through the <i>tefillah</i> of the man of great power, through which he extracts all the <i>da&rsquo;as</i> and the compassion that the <i>Sitra Achara</i> has swallowed, in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;The wealth he swallowed he shall vomit up.&rdquo;</span> And then the <i>da&rsquo;as</i> is revealed, in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;For the earth shall be full of the knowledge of Hashem, as the waters cover the sea.&rdquo;</span> And this is the aspect of <i>ananei d&rsquo;shafchei maya</i> (clouds that pour forth water), etc., the aspect of thunder, etc.; see there well in the aforementioned teaching.</p>

<p class="para">And this is the aspect of the waters of the <i>mikveh</i>, which are the aspect of the waters of <i>da&rsquo;as</i> and compassion that are revealed through the aspect of thunder, through which rains come, the aspect of <i>ananei d&rsquo;shafchei maya</i>. And from these waters is made the <i>mikveh</i>, where they are purified from the contamination of the serpent, from the aforementioned blemish that comes from the blemish of compassion, etc., as mentioned above. For the essential <i>tikkun</i> is through this, as is understood in the aforementioned teaching; understand well.</p>

<h3 class="oas-heading" id="oas-7">Oas Zayin</h3>

<p class="para">And this is the aspect of the wells that Yitzchak dug, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And Yitzchak returned and dug the wells of water that they had dug in the days of Avraham his father, and the Philistines had stopped them up&rdquo;</span> <span class="source-ref">(Bereishis 26:18)</span>. For in truth, the digging of the wells is the aspect of the revelation of <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;For the earth shall be full of the knowledge of Hashem, as the waters cover the sea,&rdquo;</span> as mentioned above. And the essential revelation of the waters of <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, which is the aspect of wells of water, is through <i>chesed</i> (kindness), the aspect of Avraham. For <i>da&rsquo;as</i> is the aspect of compassion, as is explained in the aforementioned teaching. And therefore Avraham dug the wells.</p>

<p class="para">But all the wells that were dug in the days of Avraham &mdash; the Philistines stopped them up and filled them with earth. For sometimes they [the forces of the Other Side] suckle from the compassion, and then the compassion is blemished and the <i>da&rsquo;as</i> is blemished, as mentioned above in the aforementioned teaching. For in the days of Avraham, the contamination of the serpent had not yet been fully refined, as is brought. And therefore Yishma&rsquo;el came forth from him.</p>

<p class="para">And therefore the <i>tikkun</i> was through Yitzchak, for Yitzchak is the aspect of <i>din</i> (judgment) and he is the aspect of <i>tefillah</i> in the aspect of <i>din</i>, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And Yitzchak went out to converse in the field toward evening&rdquo;</span> <span class="source-ref">(Bereishis 24:63)</span> &mdash; for he instituted the afternoon prayer, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said &mdash; which is the aspect of <i>tefillah</i> in the aspect of <i>din</i>. And through this specifically one extracts all the vitality, etc., from the <i>Sitra Achara</i>, and the waters of <i>da&rsquo;as</i> are revealed, etc., in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;For the earth shall be full of the knowledge, as the waters,&rdquo;</span> etc., in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;You broke apart the sea with Your might; You shattered the heads of the sea-serpents upon the waters,&rdquo;</span> as mentioned above in the aforementioned teaching.</p>

<p class="para">And therefore Yitzchak rectified the wells, which are the aspect of the revelation of the <i>da&rsquo;as</i> of Avraham that the Philistines had damaged, as mentioned above. And Yitzchak, who is the aspect of <i>tefillah</i> in the aspect of <i>din</i>, rectified this, in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And Yitzchak returned and dug the wells of water,&rdquo;</span> etc. For the essential <i>tikkun</i> is through the aspect of Yitzchak, etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<p class="para">And this is the aspect of why we mention the might of the rains in the blessing of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;You are mighty&rdquo;</span> (<i>Atah Gibor</i>). For they are called <i>g&rsquo;vuros g&rsquo;shamim</i> (the might of the rains), because the rains, which are the waters of <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, come specifically through the aspect of the might of Yitzchak, through the aspect of <i>tefillah</i> in the aspect of <i>din</i>, through which <i>da&rsquo;as</i> is revealed, as mentioned above. For through this come the thunders, the aspect of <i>ananei d&rsquo;shafchei maya</i>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p class="para">And this is the aspect of the <i>mikveh</i>, which is the aspect of the waters of <i>da&rsquo;as</i> that come through the aforementioned <i>tikkun</i>. For the <i>mikveh</i> is made through rainwater, which is the aspect of <i>g&rsquo;vuros g&rsquo;shamim</i>, or from a well and a spring, which are the aspect of the wells of Yitzchak. For specifically through the aspect of the might of Yitzchak are the waters of <i>da&rsquo;as</i> and compassion revealed, the aspect of the <i>mikveh</i>, as mentioned above. And this is the essential <i>tikkun</i>, for it is the aspect of <i>tefillah</i> in the aspect of <i>din</i> of the man of great power, as mentioned above in the aforementioned teaching. And therefore through this specifically they are purified from the contamination of the serpent, etc., as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of the immersion in the <i>mikveh</i>, whether of the <i>niddah</i> or of the gentiles when they convert. For through this they emerge from the aspect of <i>din</i>, which is the contamination of the serpent, the blemish of the desire of adultery, and they are included in the totality of compassion and <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, upon which the essential holiness of the union depends, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3 class="oas-heading" id="oas-8">Oas Ches</h3>

<p class="para">And therefore the Kohein, who is the aspect of the ultimate compassion and <i>da&rsquo;as</i> &mdash; as is brought, that the Kohein is the aspect of great <i>chesed</i> (kindness), for the Kohein is the first of the three aforementioned brains, of the three aforementioned kinds of compassion &mdash; therefore the Kohein is warned even more regarding the holiness of the union, and must distance himself from the aspect of <i>din</i> more and more. And even among Israelites themselves, wherever there is any hold of <i>din</i> whatsoever, she is forbidden to him.</p>

<p class="para">And this is the aspect of those disqualified for the <i>Kehunah</i> (priesthood), which are: a divorcee, a <i>zonah</i> (harlot), and a <i>chalalah</i> (profaned woman) &mdash; all of whom are in the aspect of <i>din</i>. And even though they are of the seed of Israel and are in truth permitted to a [regular] Yisra&rsquo;el, nevertheless, since there is a hold of <i>din</i> in them, they are therefore forbidden to a Kohein, who is the ultimate of compassion and <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of a captive woman, who is forbidden to a Kohein. For since <i>din</i> has taken hold of her to the point that she came into captivity, she is therefore forbidden to the Kohein, who is the ultimate of compassion. For the essential holiness of the union depends on the aspect of compassion, which is the aspect of <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, as mentioned above.</p>

<h3 class="oas-heading" id="oas-9">Oas Tes</h3>

<p class="para">And this is the aspect of: Pinchas did not become a Kohein until he killed Zimri. For through his killing of Zimri, Pinchas then effected the <i>tikkun</i> through <i>tefillah</i> in the aspect of <i>din</i>, as is explained in the aforementioned teaching, in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And Pinchas stood up and prayed&rdquo;</span> <span class="source-ref">(Tehillim 106:30)</span>. And then, specifically through this, the ultimate compassion and <i>da&rsquo;as</i> was revealed, the aspect of <i>ananei d&rsquo;shafchei maya</i> (clouds that pour forth water) &mdash; which is the aspect of the waters of the <i>mikveh</i>, which is the ultimate of compassion and <i>da&rsquo;as</i> that is revealed specifically through the aspect of the might of Yitzchak, as mentioned above.</p>

<p class="para">And therefore Pinchas then merited the <i>Kehunah</i>, which is the ultimate of compassion. For specifically through <i>tefillah</i> in the aspect of <i>din</i> of the man of great power, like Pinchas, is the essential <i>tikkun</i> effected. And then specifically comes the essential revelation of compassion and <i>da&rsquo;as</i>, through which converts are made, and thunders are made, the aspect of <i>ananei d&rsquo;shafchei maya</i> &mdash; that is, the waters of <i>da&rsquo;as</i> and compassion. And through this one merits the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;a river goes forth from Eden&rdquo;</span> <span class="source-ref">(Bereishis 2:10)</span>, which is the aspect of the voice of the worthy reprover, through which everything is purified and rectified, speedily in our days, <i>Amein</i>.</p>

<p class="para"><i>Halacha 3 &mdash; In Hilchos Pirya V&rsquo;Rivya, Halacha 3, from Oas Tes-Zayin onward.</i></p>

